{"records":[{"id":"ptx3dzs926","title":"NGS data of CRISPR/dCas9 activation screen with CDK4/6 inhibitor Palbociclib in bladder cancer","description":"We used a genome-scale functional genomics approach to determine the mechanisms of resistance to PD0332991. Transcriptional activation was performed using the synergistic activation mediator (SAM) CRISPR-dCas9 library. Work flow: a) T24 cells with stably transduced SAM components. b) Low MOI lentiviral transduction of  amplified sgRNA library.  c)antibiotic selection for transduced  cells. e) divide cells into control(vehicle) and PD 7 days treatment. f) NGS of PCR amplicons. g) Comparison of sgRNA counts in control and treatment conditions.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-06-01T04:24:44.789Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ptx3dzs926","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ptx3dzs926"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Zhichao","last_name":"Tong","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"vs9fwhbcvj","title":"Genome-wide Brie CAD5 Surface PrPC - Differentiated PrPC High","description":"These are the raw .fastq files from NGS runs of the genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 KO library (Brie) performed in differentiated CAD5 cells.  They are labeled Brie_PrPC_High to indicate that these sgRNA sequences were captured in the \"PrPC High\" populations during FACS.  Bioinformatic analysis was performed using the MAGeCK-VISPR and MAGeCKFlute pipelines using the biological replicates function to compare between \"PrP Low\" and \"PrP High\" samples.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-13T07:36:42.171Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/vs9fwhbcvj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/vs9fwhbcvj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kathryn","last_name":"Beauchemin","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"1R37NS125431"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"P20-GM113132 "},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS118796"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS117276"}],"categories":["Prion","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"5pfdty7zd6","title":"Genome-wide Brie CAD5 Surface PrPC  - Undifferentiated","description":"These are the raw .fastq files from NGS runs of the genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 KO library (Brie) performed in undifferentiated CAD5 cells.  They are labeled Brie_PrPC_Low or Brie_PrPC_High to indicate whether these sgRNA sequences were captured in the \"PrPC Low\" or \"PrPC High\" populations during FACS.  Bioinformatic analysis was performed using the MAGeCK-VISPR and MAGeCKFlute pipelines using the biological replicates function to compare \"PrP Low\" and \"PrP High\" samples directly.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-13T07:36:32.252Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/5pfdty7zd6","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/5pfdty7zd6"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kathryn","last_name":"Beauchemin","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"P20-GM113132 "},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"1R37NS125431"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS117276"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS118796"}],"categories":["Prion","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"p5t6d78zn8","title":"Genome-wide Brie CAD5 Surface PrPC - Differentiated PrPC Low","description":"These are the raw .fastq files from NGS runs of the genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 KO library (Brie) performed in differentiated CAD5 cells.  They are labeled Brie_PrPC_Low  to indicate that these sgRNA sequences were captured in the \"PrPC Low\" populations during FACS.  Bioinformatic analysis was performed using the MAGeCK-VISPR and MAGeCKFlute pipelines using the biological replicates function to compare between \"PrP Low\" and \"PrP High\" samples.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-13T07:36:58.456Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/p5t6d78zn8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/p5t6d78zn8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kathryn","last_name":"Beauchemin","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"1R37NS125431"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS118796"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"P20-GM113132 "},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS117276"}],"categories":["Prion","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"9rc2n4bkmv","title":"Functional interrogation of a SARS-CoV-2 host protein interactome identifies unique and shared coronavirus host factors. Hoffmann et al.","description":"The ongoing SARS-CoV-2 pandemic has devastated the global economy and claimed more than one million lives, presenting an urgent global health crisis. To identify host factors required for infection by SARS-CoV-2 and seasonal coronaviruses, we designed a focused high-coverage CRISPR-Cas9 library targeting 332 members of a recently published SARS-CoV-2 protein interactome. We leveraged the compact nature of this library to systematically screen SARS-CoV-2 at two physiologically relevant temperatures (33 ºC and 37 ºC) along with three related coronaviruses (HCoV-229E, HCoV-NL63, and HCoV-OC43), allowing us to probe this interactome at a much higher resolution relative to genome scale studies. This approach yielded several new insights, including unexpected virus-specific differences in Rab GTPase requirements and GPI anchor biosynthesis, as well as identification of multiple pan-coronavirus factors involved in cholesterol homeostasis. This coronavirus essentiality catalog could inform ongoing drug development efforts aimed at intercepting and treating COVID-19, and help prepare for future coronavirus outbreaks.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-11-25T19:01:19.445Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/9rc2n4bkmv","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/9rc2n4bkmv"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"JT","last_name":"Poirier","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Coronavirus","Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2","COVID-19"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"tmkn3zsjts","title":"Secondary Library Validation Surface PrPC - Undifferentiated","description":"These are the raw .fastq files from NGS runs of the custom secondary validation CRISPR/Cas9 KO library performed in undifferentiated  CAD5 cells.  They are labeled Brie_PrPC_Low or Brie_PrPC_High to indicate whether these sgRNA sequences were captured in the \"PrPC Low\" or \"PrPC High\" populations during FACS.  Bioinformatic analysis was performed using the MAGeCK-VISPR and MAGeCKFlute pipelines using the paired function to compare high and low samples directly.  ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-13T07:36:24.211Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/tmkn3zsjts","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/tmkn3zsjts"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kathryn","last_name":"Beauchemin","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"P20-GM113132 "},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"1R37NS125431"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS117276"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS118796"}],"categories":["Prion","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"jb89dp34d8","title":"Secondary Library Validation Surface PrPC - Differentiated","description":"These are the raw .fastq files from NGS runs of the custom secondary validation CRISPR/Cas9 KO library performed in  differentiated CAD5 cells.  They are labeled Brie_PrPC_Low or Brie_PrPC_High to indicate whether these sgRNA sequences were captured in the \"PrPC Low\" or \"PrPC High\" populations during FACS.  Bioinformatic analysis was performed using the MAGeCK-VISPR and MAGeCKFlute pipelines using the paired function to compare high and low samples directly.  ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-06-13T07:36:18.673Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/jb89dp34d8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/jb89dp34d8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kathryn","last_name":"Beauchemin","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS118796"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS117276"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"1R37NS125431"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"P20-GM113132 "}],"categories":["Prion","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"jv32cvpn3r","title":"CAD5 Brie Library Quality Control","description":"Whole-genome mouse CRISPR-KO Brie library in CAD5 cells - quality control run.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-10-10T14:21:40.826Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/jv32cvpn3r","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/jv32cvpn3r"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kathryn","last_name":"Beauchemin","orcid":null},{"first_name":"surachai","last_name":"supattapone","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS118796"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"R01NS117276"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01s5ya894","name":"National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke","grant_id":"1R37NS125431"}],"categories":["CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"3jgy6bw5zz","title":"Rapid iPSC inclusionopathy models shed light on formation, consequence and molecular subtype of α-synuclein inclusions - CRISPR Screening Data","description":"Raw CRISPR sequencing read counts with sgRNA sequences from:\nRapid iPSC inclusionopathy models shed light on formation, consequence and molecular subtype of α-synuclein inclusions\nFigure 8","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-05-31T08:41:14.454Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/3jgy6bw5zz","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/3jgy6bw5zz"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Isabel","last_name":"Lam","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Timothy","last_name":"Martin","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["High-Throughput Screening"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"j5n84znyvf","title":"Tumor-Educated Hepatocytes Drive Immune Evasion in Colorectal Cancer Liver Metastasis Through KLK5 Secretion","description":"1.RNA-seq data generated from paired primary colorectal cancer lesions and matched hepatic metastatic lesions obtained from the same patients with colorectal cancer liver metastasis (CRLM).\n2.RNA-seq data of THLE-2 cells after co-culture with RKO cells and of control (monocultured) THLE-2 cells.\n3. RNA-seq data of RKO cells after co-culture with THLE-2 cells and of control (monocultured) RKO cells.\n4. LC–MS data for protein identification in conditioned-medium supernatants from control THLE-2 cells and tumor-educated THLE-2 cells.\n5. CRISPR screening for KLK5 substrates.\n6. List of sgRNA sequences used for CRISPR screening.\n7. LC–MS data for the identification of lysine lactylation sites on PD-L1 protein.\n8. LC–MS data for the identification of lysine lactylation sites on PD-L1 protein.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-09-22T17:55:50.043Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/j5n84znyvf","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/j5n84znyvf"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jiaxi","last_name":"Li","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Biology","Metastatic Colorectal Cancer"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":79799,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":86,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":79799,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":79612,"restricted":47,"embargoed":140},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":1306},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":441},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Center","count":322},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":302},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6